// A literal written into one lane of a varying that is otherwise passed
// straight through (literal-lane-insert).
//
// Until 2026-09-02 the default path peeled the VecInsert chain, resolved
// the store's source inward to `color`, and then emitted ONE full-width
// MOV of that varying - dropping `c.x = 0.5` in silence.  Exit 0, a
// well-formed container, and an input mask that correctly described the
// ucode, which was missing a line of the source.  The completeness guard
// (post-discard-colour) cannot see this one: the varying IS read; it is the
// LITERAL that goes missing.
//
// Reference compiler, for this shader:
//
//     MOVR R0.yzw, f[TEX0];
//     MOVR R0.x,   {0x3f000000(0.5), 0, 0, 0}.x;
//
// The base MOV is masked to the lanes the insert does not write, and the
// override follows it.  Ours is byte-identical to that.
void main(float4 color : TEXCOORD0,
          out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    float4 c = color;
    c.x = 0.5;
    oColor = c;
}
